1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,030
Cinderella

2
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:10,560
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:19,910
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,280
No.

5
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,900
What is not?

6
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:34,030
Let's go. I will tell you on the way.

7
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:36,720
Let's go. I will tell you everything.

8
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,490
Welcome.

9
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,200
10,000,000 won.

10
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:33,990
Fine. You are just a man worth just that much.

11
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:43,580
Come out. I will tell you everything.

12
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,310
Episode 9
She's not at the cooperative there either.

13
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:13,010
Is that so? She has always been in the lab and she didn't even leave a note, where did she go?

14
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:14,500
She's also not picking up her phone, right?

15
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,070
Yeah. She's not answering.

16
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:20,210
Okay. Go to the house and keep searching.

17
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:23,570
Gi Hoon went home to look.

18
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:48,110
A blue curtain

19
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:53,680
This room which doesn't even have a single bright lipstick.

20
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:59,410
This is a room of a 26-year-old woman.

21
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:02,370
How could it be...

22
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:07,000
that there isn't even a little stuffed animal in here.

23
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:15,680
That bad girl who I thought didn't know how to smile.

24
00:03:28,090 --> 00:03:31,330
Where did she go?

25
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:35,760
Somewhere, is that bad girl smiling again?

26
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:53,970
Song Eun Jo is Han Jeong Woo's woman forever.

27
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:07,610
Oppa, you were here.

28
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,290
What is this?

29
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:25,410
Song Eun Jo is Han Jeong Woo's woman forever.

30
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:32,560
Han Jeong Woo? Is that your roomate?

31
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:36,080
Song Eun Jo...

32
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:40,900
So he knew Eun Jo

33
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,920
ever since she was Song Eun Jo.

34
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:05,800
♫ Again today my memory led me astray ♫

35
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:10,630
♫ I who am strolling at the end of the street ♫

36
00:05:13,050 --> 00:05:20,290
♫ Where you can't hold me again ♫

37
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:25,710
♫  I ask again about the way ♫

38
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:29,340
♫ Saying that I want to see you ♫

39
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:34,680
♫  and hold you again ♫

40
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:40,610
♫ While looking at heaven I am praying ♫

41
00:05:40,610 --> 00:05:44,370
♫ It must be you ♫

42
00:05:44,370 --> 00:05:47,960
♫ I cannot be without you ♫

43
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:54,880
♫ Like this for another day, month or year ♫

44
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:58,550
♫ I don't mind even if I am hurt. ♫

45
00:05:58,550 --> 00:06:02,520
♫  I don't mind if my heart breaks ♫

46
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:06,980
♫ because, yes, you are the only one I love ♫

47
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:10,750
Will you hold on to me?

48
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:18,140
If you hold on to me, I think I will be able to stop now.

49
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:24,010
Before I board the train,

50
00:06:24,010 --> 00:06:28,210
hold on to me, Eun Joo.

51
00:06:32,790 --> 00:06:36,120
The bad girl that I love.

52
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:39,310
I knew you were very tough.

53
00:06:40,370 --> 00:06:45,820
But I didn't know you would easily ignore my earnest plea for you to hold on to me.

54
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,200
I really didn't know.

55
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:04,040
It's all over. Believe me.

56
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:07,230
Right? It's done.

57
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:14,180
You said you would die. You threatened me that you would die.

58
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:17,620
I didn't want you to die so I ended it.

59
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:21,360
I am not fooling you for a while but it's for real.

60
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,200
So until now,

61
00:07:24,490 --> 00:07:27,950
all this while, you two met?

62
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,580
Yes.

63
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:35,160
What are you saying? We didn't meet for three years in between.

64
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,180
Won't you shut it?

65
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:43,570
So if you don't meet now

66
00:07:43,570 --> 00:07:47,590
if it's the end as you said

67
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:54,490
then you could meet after some time again.

68
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:59,160
You won't believe me even if I say I won't.

69
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:04,460
How could I? Would you believe it if you were me?

70
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:08,860
You lie whenever you open your mouth, then cover it up with another lie.

71
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:13,550
What the truth is, can you even differentiate it?

72
00:08:13,550 --> 00:08:15,910
Do you even have sincerity?

73
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:18,030
Shut up and listen to me, wench.

74
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:22,290
You thought you were able to fool everyone without being caught, you thought no one knew, right?

75
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:25,620
You thought it was easy to make a naive man a fool?

76
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:29,730
I... got rid of that man.

77
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:34,420
I gave him money so that he will get off me.

78
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:40,780
If I gave money to get him off it means I made a resolve already.

79
00:08:48,990 --> 00:08:52,300
What is this? What does this mean?

80
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:57,650
I will get off. I will not take this money and get off.

81
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:05,020
No matter how bad I am, I know how to be ashamed.

82
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:26,270
To you, I already showed you everything.

83
00:09:28,330 --> 00:09:30,680
I have nothing to show.

84
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:41,500
This brat who followed to see me die. Bad wench.

85
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,590
Are you relieved?

86
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:13,210
I could have gotten this though.

87
00:10:13,210 --> 00:10:16,300
How could you make this everyday? It's tiring.

88
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:20,140
It's not tiring. Hurry and drink it.

89
00:10:41,310 --> 00:10:45,330
I don't like you, Honey, coming to work everyday.

90
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:48,450
It would be best to leave it to someone, and for now

91
00:10:48,450 --> 00:10:52,970
stay at home taking easy walks at times while resting.

92
00:10:55,330 --> 00:10:58,840
I'm going. If you can't go home for dinner tonight,

93
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:02,120
call me. I'll bring you something.

94
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:25,720
Go with Hyo Seon's father.

95
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:29,260
A problem came up at the factory. Take him home.

96
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:32,330
Think of any excuse. No matter what, he can't be here.

97
00:11:32,330 --> 00:11:37,970
Don't let him pick up any calls either. Hyo Seon's father can't undergo any shock anymore.

98
00:11:37,970 --> 00:11:39,900
Why? What's wrong?

99
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:42,990
Take him with you and go on a trip for a few days.

100
00:11:42,990 --> 00:11:46,460
That'll be better. Please, Mom.

101
00:11:51,090 --> 00:11:54,840
Please tell me why you suddenly can't supply us with rice anymore.

102
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:59,110
No, but if you suddenly—

103
00:11:59,110 --> 00:12:02,930
Hello? Hello?

104
00:12:07,370 --> 00:12:11,670
What did they say? Why can't they supply rice for us?

105
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:21,340
Wait... Can't we purchase rice from somewhere else?

106
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:22,950
Didn't you read the contract?

107
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:27,090
It says we can only use organic rice from the Gyeonggi-do area.

108
00:12:36,530 --> 00:12:40,420
How can you do this? How can you suddenly do this?

109
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:43,310
This is not the first deal you've done with our Dae Seong True Wine Makers.

110
00:12:43,310 --> 00:12:46,660
How can you just suddenly break your promise overnight?

111
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:50,470
This is a breach of contract!

112
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:56,000
Breach of contract? What breach? Did we even sign a contract?

113
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
What did you say?

114
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:02,480
If we signed a contract, then there should be a physical contract. Bring it over.

115
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:05,760
We have been supplying rice to you all this time,

116
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:09,750
but that's not a contract. We provided the rice first,

117
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:13,230
and President Goo Dae Seong would pay us with revenue from rice wine sales later.

118
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:17,090
We've been supplying the rice without a contract all this time and you're not even thankful.

119
00:13:17,090 --> 00:13:19,400
Young people these days...

120
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:25,330
Then who's getting the rice originally meant for us?

121
00:13:25,330 --> 00:13:30,390
I don't know. I'm off work now, so let's leave it at that.

122
00:13:31,230 --> 00:13:32,860
Managing Director...

123
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:37,440
- Excuse me, Ajusshi!
- Wait, Ajusshi.

124
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:41,550
You don't remember me?

125
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:43,720
I haven't been here for a while now,

126
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:47,900
but I came here with my dad to play when I was young.

127
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:51,250
You don't remember?

128
00:13:51,250 --> 00:13:56,320
I'm Hyo Seon! You said I was pretty and even bought me candy.

129
00:13:56,320 --> 00:14:01,270
You even fed me rice wine as a joke before!

130
00:14:01,270 --> 00:14:04,500
Oh! That daughter.

131
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:06,740
Yes! I'm that daughter.

132
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:10,840
Ajusshi, don't leave

133
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:15,370
and just have one cup of rice wine with us. Please?

134
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:21,060
Thank you, Ajusshi. We won't take much of your time.

135
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:24,260
Cheers!

136
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:34,020
Ajusshi, have one more cup.

137
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:37,230
I shouldn't drink any more.

138
00:14:43,590 --> 00:14:47,280
- Pour me one too.
- All right.

139
00:14:48,510 --> 00:14:53,590
Why is a kid like you so good at drinking?

140
00:15:01,070 --> 00:15:04,590
Please accept one more cup!

141
00:15:04,590 --> 00:15:09,200
Ajusshi, who bought the rice

142
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:12,580
that was meant for us?

143
00:15:25,190 --> 00:15:28,260
Why don't we meet that person tomorrow instead?

144
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,340
We don't have time.

145
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:32,370
It's night time.

146
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:36,250
We're going now. The days are flying by.

147
00:15:36,250 --> 00:15:40,410
Even if we get the rice tomorrow, we may not even be able to make the deadline.

148
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:46,940
Are you going to argue with him this late at night just like you did with the director just now?

149
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:51,290
In adults' eyes, they will only consider that disrespectful.

150
00:15:56,290 --> 00:16:01,800
Oppa, did I do well today?

151
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:04,380
I did well, didn't I?

152
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,010
Yes, you did well, Hyo Seon.

153
00:16:07,010 --> 00:16:13,250
As long as Oppa is watching, I can do everything well.

154
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:24,160
I'll go with Hyo Seon tomorrow.

155
00:16:25,130 --> 00:16:26,730
I'll do it.

156
00:16:26,730 --> 00:16:29,040
You don't trust Hyo Seon?

157
00:16:31,690 --> 00:16:34,430
She's more capable than you are.

158
00:16:36,470 --> 00:16:39,450
You can't find your way to others' hearts.

159
00:16:45,470 --> 00:16:46,980
Is that so?

160
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:51,300
You won't get any answers with the way you act.

161
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,740
Is that so?

162
00:16:59,870 --> 00:17:03,130
You're a pro at having people lock their hearts up.

163
00:17:05,230 --> 00:17:07,880
Stop the car.

164
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:10,800
Stop the car?

165
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:12,650
Stop the car.

166
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:35,670
There's just one thing I want to ask you.

167
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:50,540
Back then ... when I left,

168
00:18:53,370 --> 00:18:55,900
why didn't you come to the train station?

169
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:05,370
You didn't get my letter?

170
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:14,610
I have no idea what you're talking about.

171
00:19:14,610 --> 00:19:17,570
I told Hyo Seon to give you a letter

172
00:19:18,890 --> 00:19:21,730
asking you to come to the train station.

173
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:32,750
Did Hyo Seon, perhaps, not give it to you?

174
00:19:41,630 --> 00:19:43,500
I got it.

175
00:19:44,990 --> 00:19:46,890
You did?

176
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:51,700
I got it.

177
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:54,410
You got it...?

178
00:19:54,410 --> 00:19:58,520
I don't even remember if I ripped it up or burned it after reading it.

179
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:01,510
Is that something I have to remember?

180
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:08,860
You didn't come even after reading it?

181
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:11,140
Stop acting like a beggar.

182
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:17,420
- What did you say?
- What are you begging for?

183
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:22,490
You want to relive the past with me? There's nothing I can give you.

184
00:20:22,490 --> 00:20:27,400
Stop asking me about the past! I told you there's nothing!

185
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:52,690
♫ Even if there are wounds left in my heart now ♫

186
00:20:55,700 --> 00:21:02,000
♫ I am told to forget about you ♫

187
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:06,900
♫ But even if I bite my lips and bear it ♫

188
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,580
You didn't get my letter?

189
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:15,190
♫ You are the only one who is my person ♫

190
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:22,440
♫ I am living day after day ♫

191
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:25,910
♫ In your name  ♫

192
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:31,210
♫ when tears appear again, woo  ♫

193
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:36,240
♫ I can't bear it  ♫

194
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:39,350
♫ So I can't laugh ♫

195
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:48,300
♫ I'll call out your name again. ♫

196
00:22:00,290 --> 00:22:04,920
Hyo Seon didn't give it to you?

197
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:08,270
As long as Oppa is watching,

198
00:22:08,270 --> 00:22:11,830
I can do everything well.

199
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,050
One...two...

200
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:40,090
Honey, look here.

201
00:22:46,850 --> 00:22:49,240
It's delicious, isn't it?

202
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:11,260
Drink it before it cools.

203
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:31,910
What is it? You want to make a call?

204
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:34,430
I'm wondering how the factory is doing.

205
00:23:37,810 --> 00:23:42,680
Just forget about the factory while we're here. The children can handle it.

206
00:23:48,250 --> 00:23:51,950
Let's go over there. There's a nice place over there.

207
00:23:51,950 --> 00:23:54,870
- I'll take it.
- It's okay. Let's go.

208
00:24:01,350 --> 00:24:08,830
Go faster! Faster, faster!

209
00:24:08,860 --> 00:24:12,850
Run! Run!

210
00:24:12,850 --> 00:24:17,210
Faster! Faster!

211
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:22,400
Giddy-up! Run fast!

212
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:25,400
We can't export.

213
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,940
What do you mean?

214
00:24:26,940 --> 00:24:31,610
The person who bought all the rice says they'll sell it to us for three times the cost.

215
00:24:31,610 --> 00:24:32,660
What did you say?

216
00:24:32,660 --> 00:24:38,300
If we pay three times the cost for the rice we need to make the rice wine, it'll cost more to make than the profit for selling it.

217
00:24:38,300 --> 00:24:40,270
I'm going to tell Dad right now.

218
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:42,240
No. Don't say anything to him.

219
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:44,240
How can we not tell him about it?

220
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:48,440
Just come home without saying anything to him! Hang up.

221
00:24:52,410 --> 00:24:58,250
Wow, so strong!

222
00:24:58,250 --> 00:25:07,290
Now, strong! Wow! So fun!

223
00:25:20,890 --> 00:25:24,370
You're not going to answer me even if I ask what's wrong.

224
00:25:24,370 --> 00:25:28,860
Right. I won't answer. You're being bothersome. Go outside.

225
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:33,660
Okay. But drink first. I'll leave after I see you drink it.

226
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:37,990
I'll drink it, so leave.

227
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,260
I'll leave after I see it.

228
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:48,320
That honey tea is good for mental and physical stability. And it's good for your upper digestive...

229
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:50,770
I said to go outside.

230
00:25:53,540 --> 00:25:58,380
If you tell me to die, I could die.

231
00:25:58,380 --> 00:26:02,350
You have to eat in front of me the things I tell you to eat.

232
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:08,680
Oh, man. What's so hard about drinking that?

233
00:26:30,900 --> 00:26:33,130
Are you sleeping well?

234
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:40,960
Where are you going?

235
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:46,330
Yes, I understand. I'll leave now, so you guys go on to the factory. Okay.

236
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:50,950
Is there something wrong, Honey?

237
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:57,790
You've lost all color in your face. Are you okay?

238
00:26:57,790 --> 00:27:01,150
I'm okay. Let's get going now.

239
00:27:09,570 --> 00:27:14,100
I said I'm okay. If you treat me like a patient, I'll get upset at you.

240
00:27:14,100 --> 00:27:18,390
I'm not treating you like a patient. It's because I like holding onto you.

241
00:27:19,620 --> 00:27:21,420
Is that so?

242
00:27:24,300 --> 00:27:26,310
Thank you.

243
00:27:39,150 --> 00:27:41,500
Please let me see the documents.

244
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:47,660
This is the export contract. Do you think a loan will be possible?

245
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:58,450
We'll let you know the results of the review by tomorrow morning at the latest.

246
00:28:26,510 --> 00:28:30,070
Do you need money?

247
00:28:33,900 --> 00:28:35,830
Use my money.

248
00:28:37,260 --> 00:28:41,460
My entire life's savings that I gave you. Use it.

249
00:28:45,020 --> 00:28:50,530
Didn't I tell you? I said I'll be responsible for your life.

250
00:28:59,110 --> 00:29:04,910
Hey. Does that even make sense? You're going to purchase it at three times the original cost?

251
00:29:04,910 --> 00:29:08,960
What would be left over after that?

252
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:11,960
What's the difference between doing that and just ending our business now?

253
00:29:11,960 --> 00:29:16,220
Daeseong's reputation already hit rock bottom because of our last incident.

254
00:29:16,220 --> 00:29:19,820
If we can't fulfill our orders this time, it'll be nearly impossible to rebuild our name.

255
00:29:19,820 --> 00:29:24,500
So what? You went to the bank as you pleased with a contract?

256
00:29:24,500 --> 00:29:28,490
You want to take out a loan? What happens if we can't pay it back?!

257
00:29:28,490 --> 00:29:30,340
What will happen if we can't repay the loan?!

258
00:29:30,340 --> 00:29:34,570
Why can't we repay it? If we successfully get this order through, we can get back on our feet again.

259
00:29:34,570 --> 00:29:36,530
How do you know that will happen?!

260
00:29:36,530 --> 00:29:40,190
I know, so why don't you know?

261
00:29:40,190 --> 00:29:42,910
How is it possible that you don't know it?

262
00:29:42,910 --> 00:29:44,100
What did you say?

263
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:47,550
The "Dae Seong" of "Dae Seong Cham Do Ga", is your father's name.

264
00:29:47,550 --> 00:29:51,560
Even before you were born, people drank rice wine associated with your father's name.

265
00:29:51,560 --> 00:29:55,200
This time if it's known that Dae Seong Cham Do Ga failed to fulfill its promise to fill in this order,

266
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:57,360
your father's name will be ruined.

267
00:29:57,360 --> 00:30:00,170
Can you allow that to happen? Your own father's name?

268
00:30:00,170 --> 00:30:03,820
Stop acting like you're thinking of my father!

269
00:30:04,730 --> 00:30:08,680
You think you care more than I do?

270
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:11,450
More than me?

271
00:30:11,450 --> 00:30:15,510
Goo Eun Jo cares more than Goo Hyo Seon?

272
00:30:15,510 --> 00:30:18,140
Don't be hypocritical!

273
00:30:18,140 --> 00:30:21,160
Don't say that it's to protect my dad's name.

274
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:27,870
It's better for you be honest and say it's so you'll have more to take later.

275
00:30:31,820 --> 00:30:33,710
Isn't that it?

276
00:30:35,900 --> 00:30:37,860
It's not?

277
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:41,730
If it isn't, say it isn't true.

278
00:30:42,630 --> 00:30:44,940
Why can't you say it?

279
00:30:45,540 --> 00:30:48,110
I said, say it!

280
00:30:48,130 --> 00:30:55,550
How can you know what's in my heart so well when I don't even know.

281
00:30:56,470 --> 00:30:57,540
What?

282
00:30:57,540 --> 00:31:02,530
What are you so afraid of that you keep asking me to reveal my inner thoughts?

283
00:31:02,530 --> 00:31:04,210
Who said I was afraid?

284
00:31:04,210 --> 00:31:08,010
How much I'll take away... is that what you're afraid of?

285
00:31:08,010 --> 00:31:12,680
No. Or is it that you're afraid of me becoming a more important person than you?

286
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:17,900
If that's not it either, then are you afraid that I'll take everything away and leave nothing for you?

287
00:31:17,900 --> 00:31:21,690
- Do you think I'll let you take it?
- Let's just assume I had other intentions.

288
00:31:21,690 --> 00:31:27,010
Even if I did, I wouldn't tell you. This is immature and unbearable!

289
00:31:27,010 --> 00:31:32,670
The reason I'm this patient with you is because you are your father's daughter.

290
00:31:34,950 --> 00:31:38,650
Where do you think you're going? Say that again.

291
00:31:38,650 --> 00:31:41,640
Let go.

292
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:48,430
What? Immature and unbearable?

293
00:31:48,430 --> 00:31:51,070
Immature and unbearable!

294
00:31:51,070 --> 00:31:53,210
You're so unbelievably immature

295
00:31:53,210 --> 00:31:57,040
I'm going crazy just imagining the unbearable consequences of your actions!

296
00:31:57,040 --> 00:32:02,230
What? The results of my immaturity?

297
00:32:05,580 --> 00:32:06,830
What do you mean?

298
00:32:06,830 --> 00:32:12,440
That's enough. It's all in the past and I don't want to talk about it.

299
00:32:14,170 --> 00:32:16,510
I asked you what you meant.

300
00:32:25,100 --> 00:32:28,540
Do you really want to know?

301
00:32:30,630 --> 00:32:36,370
If you don't tell me, I'll kill you.

302
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:42,750
Will you really not regret it?

303
00:32:42,750 --> 00:32:47,250
Stop playing around and tell me.

304
00:32:48,860 --> 00:32:51,350
That person's letter...

305
00:32:52,730 --> 00:32:57,190
Why did you keep it and not give it to me?

306
00:32:59,770 --> 00:33:04,680
You, making me say this,

307
00:33:05,600 --> 00:33:11,810
and even standing with you is unbearable. But I'll let it go.

308
00:33:13,110 --> 00:33:18,070
Not for you but because you are your father's daughter.

309
00:33:18,070 --> 00:33:19,930
Goo Hyo Seon.

310
00:33:29,370 --> 00:33:32,150
Not giving you the letter...

311
00:33:33,450 --> 00:33:36,230
you're calling that immature, right?

312
00:33:38,870 --> 00:33:40,070
Then ...

313
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:45,190
the unbearable results of my immaturity...

314
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:49,290
What's that?

315
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:55,570
You want to fall into the gutter with me?

316
00:33:55,570 --> 00:34:01,130
Must you really listen to me say it?

317
00:34:01,130 --> 00:34:02,940
Tell me ...

318
00:34:04,610 --> 00:34:07,180
before I kill you.

319
00:34:10,270 --> 00:34:11,920
For me

320
00:34:13,570 --> 00:34:15,830
since I was born into this world...

321
00:34:17,020 --> 00:34:18,900
for the first time ...

322
00:34:22,900 --> 00:34:25,000
for the first time...

323
00:34:36,590 --> 00:34:42,440
Since nothing will change, I won't make an issue out of it anymore.

324
00:34:43,750 --> 00:34:50,550
I don't want to be the main character in a story of two stepsisters fighting over one man.

325
00:34:50,550 --> 00:34:57,170
I’ve stepped out of that story a long, long time ago. I'm not going back to it.

326
00:34:57,170 --> 00:35:01,690
So, you keep your mouth shut.

327
00:35:08,950 --> 00:35:15,050
But there's something you need to be careful about.

328
00:35:20,320 --> 00:35:22,000
That man...

329
00:35:23,230 --> 00:35:26,540
doesn't seem to have gotten over me yet.

330
00:35:29,810 --> 00:35:32,200
Isn't that funny?

331
00:35:58,060 --> 00:36:02,400
Dae Seong Cham Do Ga is passing over a bump right now.

332
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:08,040
Since they have deep roots, I believe they will be able to stand right up once they pass this bump.

333
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:11,640
As you've seen, even until just 5 years ago,

334
00:36:11,640 --> 00:36:14,630
they've grown well without a single loan from the bank.

335
00:36:14,630 --> 00:36:18,960
There's not even a speck of dust in their operations.

336
00:36:21,940 --> 00:36:25,560
Right. So, what are your plans?

337
00:36:29,730 --> 00:36:34,520
Their eldest daughter is called Eun Jo.

338
00:36:34,520 --> 00:36:36,790
She's working on developing a scientific yeast.

339
00:36:36,790 --> 00:36:42,330
She spends all day and night studying yeast to unify the taste of the rice wine.

340
00:36:42,330 --> 00:36:47,530
She's smart and a talented woman so it's only a matter of time before she succeeds.

341
00:36:47,530 --> 00:36:54,150
It's possible that the yeast that woman develops will become the core of Dae Seong Cham Do Ga.

342
00:36:54,150 --> 00:36:58,760
We must have that as well.

343
00:36:58,760 --> 00:37:02,980
I need you to find out who's behind the rice prank.

344
00:37:02,980 --> 00:37:06,960
I suspect it's the joint effort of smaller businesses,

345
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:10,250
but we need solid information to be sure.

346
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:11,970
One more thing.

347
00:37:11,970 --> 00:37:15,390
Eun Jo found out it would be hard for her to find a loan from the bank for the amount she needs,

348
00:37:15,390 --> 00:37:18,330
and is searching for funds from third-parties.

349
00:37:19,750 --> 00:37:23,850
That little one is so determined...

350
00:37:26,020 --> 00:37:32,460
I cannot allow Dae Seong to get funds from third parties. You should help them.

351
00:37:32,460 --> 00:37:36,310
It will be ours anyway.

352
00:38:04,310 --> 00:38:05,310
E-so Savings Bank

353
00:38:05,310 --> 00:38:08,580
This has the best conditions of all the ones I've looked into.

354
00:38:09,590 --> 00:38:13,540
I think we'll get the amount we need.

355
00:38:13,540 --> 00:38:15,550
Is that really true?

356
00:38:17,150 --> 00:38:19,080
It's true.

357
00:38:32,590 --> 00:38:38,280
If you've looked over everything, please stamp here.

358
00:38:43,810 --> 00:38:48,030
Loan Application

359
00:38:53,740 --> 00:38:57,010
Hey! You worked hard!

360
00:39:43,530 --> 00:39:46,660
You guys all worked hard,

361
00:39:46,660 --> 00:39:50,560
You went through a lot, Dad..

362
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:54,880
I'm going to the lab. I haven't been there for a long time.

363
00:39:57,070 --> 00:39:59,010
Eun Jo.

364
00:40:01,060 --> 00:40:04,170
Let's have lunch together.

365
00:40:04,170 --> 00:40:06,070
I don't want to.

366
00:40:08,020 --> 00:40:10,270
Unni.

367
00:40:14,850 --> 00:40:19,100
Let's eat together, okay?

368
00:40:21,300 --> 00:40:23,220
Let go.

369
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:28,790
I'm my dad's daughter.

370
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:34,980
You said you'll let it go since I'm my dad's daughter. Where are you going?

371
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,570
If you leave now,

372
00:40:37,570 --> 00:40:44,790
I have to watch my dad's heart hurt over not having fed you.

373
00:40:45,590 --> 00:40:48,790
You can't go.

374
00:40:48,790 --> 00:40:52,090
Eat and go, you evil bitch.

375
00:40:55,540 --> 00:40:58,520
I feel so good.

376
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:02,770
Whatever the results be, because you all helped me,

377
00:41:02,770 --> 00:41:06,860
I feel like I was able to blow my nose without using my hands.

378
00:41:10,770 --> 00:41:15,450
Dad, why are you talking about blowing your nose while we're eating?

379
00:41:20,330 --> 00:41:22,360
It's so delicious.

380
00:41:24,310 --> 00:41:27,850
Eun Jo, will you pour me a drink?

381
00:41:41,470 --> 00:41:43,430
Would you like one?

382
00:41:46,010 --> 00:41:52,000
- No.
- There you go again, being so cold.

383
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:55,640
All right then, I'll drink Eun Jo's alcohol.

384
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:58,960
- Gi Hoon, pour me a drink.
- Yes.

385
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:04,150
Stop drinking, you have to stop drinking,

386
00:42:23,400 --> 00:42:26,100
Do you want a drink?

387
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:37,930
Yes. Thank you, Unni.

388
00:42:57,610 --> 00:42:59,450
You take one.

389
00:43:17,860 --> 00:43:19,510
Here.

390
00:43:32,110 --> 00:43:35,580
You two...

391
00:43:47,630 --> 00:43:53,150
Oppa Gi Hoon, leave with Dad first.

392
00:43:53,150 --> 00:43:57,690
I want to have a drink with Unni today.

393
00:44:00,340 --> 00:44:02,910
That's enough. Eun Jo can't drink.

394
00:44:02,910 --> 00:44:09,460
No, I can. Let's have a drink together, Hyo Seon.

395
00:44:18,970 --> 00:44:21,050
Drink...

396
00:44:29,930 --> 00:44:31,780
You...

397
00:44:35,260 --> 00:44:41,580
Can you leave our family?

398
00:44:45,480 --> 00:44:47,620
Leave.

399
00:44:50,340 --> 00:44:52,710
Get out.

400
00:44:56,540 --> 00:44:58,330
Why?

401
00:44:59,830 --> 00:45:04,210
Because I feel like I'm going to kill you soon.

402
00:45:07,030 --> 00:45:10,640
I really hate you.

403
00:45:12,820 --> 00:45:18,300
Yet you once said you really liked me.

404
00:45:19,900 --> 00:45:22,350
I never said that.

405
00:45:24,400 --> 00:45:27,230
You never said that?

406
00:45:27,260 --> 00:45:33,900
You used to annoyingly follow me around.

407
00:45:45,400 --> 00:45:48,320
Leave.

408
00:45:48,320 --> 00:45:53,960
My officetel in Seoul is still as is.

409
00:45:55,790 --> 00:45:59,490
Someone like you can get a job anywhere.

410
00:45:59,490 --> 00:46:03,290
You'll have no problem surviving.

411
00:46:03,290 --> 00:46:09,360
If you have difficulties, I'll even give you my allowance.

412
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:13,720
Leave.

413
00:46:13,810 --> 00:46:16,920
Please leave.

414
00:46:16,920 --> 00:46:24,260
Seeing your face at home, at the company and at the factory

415
00:46:24,260 --> 00:46:30,850
every day is insufferable.

416
00:46:30,850 --> 00:46:34,240
I feel the same way.

417
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:39,990
Yeah. It's insufferable for you too.

418
00:46:41,960 --> 00:46:44,120
So leave.

419
00:46:44,120 --> 00:46:45,870
No.

420
00:46:50,550 --> 00:46:54,860
Did you think I'd agree?

421
00:46:54,860 --> 00:47:00,410
You think I'd agree really easily?

422
00:47:04,280 --> 00:47:07,590
Didn't you say let's give this a try?

423
00:47:07,590 --> 00:47:11,760
Didn't you want to compete and see who will win?

424
00:47:11,760 --> 00:47:14,850
You're the one who said all that.

425
00:47:14,860 --> 00:47:17,010
Why?

426
00:47:17,010 --> 00:47:22,370
Does it seem like you'll obviously lose,

427
00:47:22,370 --> 00:47:26,170
so you don't want to fight anymore all of a sudden?

428
00:47:30,770 --> 00:47:33,860
If you keep being like this,

429
00:47:35,930 --> 00:47:41,790
I'll really take everything away from you.

430
00:47:44,500 --> 00:47:47,080
You think I can't do it?

431
00:47:52,090 --> 00:47:57,520
Dae Seong True Wine Makers, your father...

432
00:47:59,260 --> 00:48:02,690
and even the person you like...

433
00:48:04,650 --> 00:48:07,560
I'll take them all from you.

434
00:48:09,620 --> 00:48:16,680
That's what you've been really thinking since the start...

435
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:21,900
Song Eun Jo.

436
00:48:24,010 --> 00:48:26,480
It's Goo Eun Jo.

437
00:48:28,740 --> 00:48:32,320
I'm Goo Eun Jo.

438
00:48:33,490 --> 00:48:39,080
Whether my last name is Song or Goo doesn't really matter but,

439
00:48:41,060 --> 00:48:44,540
if you keep acting like this...

440
00:48:46,130 --> 00:48:48,550
Should I?

441
00:48:48,550 --> 00:48:52,660
Should I really take it all from you?

442
00:48:52,660 --> 00:48:59,800
Should I see how much I can really take from you?

443
00:49:01,730 --> 00:49:04,900
Can I do that?

444
00:49:08,360 --> 00:49:10,850
You're so wicked.

445
00:49:22,130 --> 00:49:27,800
♫  Leaving behind the time ♫

446
00:49:27,800 --> 00:49:31,970
♫  which was buried in my heart ♫

447
00:49:31,970 --> 00:49:35,460
♫  I said I longed for you ♫

448
00:49:35,460 --> 00:49:40,070
♫  and waited for you ♫

449
00:49:44,530 --> 00:49:50,360
♫  Even my memory which turned away ♫

450
00:49:50,360 --> 00:49:54,520
♫  doesn't know that I longed for you ♫

451
00:49:54,520 --> 00:50:00,170
♫  Looking only in this direction ♫

452
00:50:00,170 --> 00:50:04,740
♫  my two eyes ♫

453
00:50:04,740 --> 00:50:09,310
♫  can't say they waited for you ♫

454
00:50:09,310 --> 00:50:17,310
♫  I can't say I'm coming back ♫

455
00:50:17,310 --> 00:50:22,570
♫  Will you who knows everthing about me ♫

456
00:50:23,700 --> 00:50:26,150
♫  who cannot forget you ♫
- Hey.

457
00:50:26,150 --> 00:50:28,910
♫  return to me? ♫

458
00:50:28,910 --> 00:50:34,500
♫  If there are tens of thousand who will just love you ♫

459
00:50:34,500 --> 00:50:39,960
♫  If I can always look at you ♫

460
00:50:39,960 --> 00:50:45,140
♫  The day I return to your side again ♫

461
00:50:45,140 --> 00:50:48,520
♫  will come again ♫

462
00:50:50,510 --> 00:50:52,320
Find these girls.

463
00:50:52,320 --> 00:50:56,880
Where on earth are they? What are they doing that they won't answer their phones or come home?

464
00:50:56,880 --> 00:51:00,280
I called the place where they were drinking during the day, and they said they left a long time ago.

465
00:51:00,280 --> 00:51:04,080
- We'll go look for them.
- These girls...

466
00:51:05,650 --> 00:51:10,790
Honey, you have a phone call. It's a Japanese person.

467
00:51:10,790 --> 00:51:12,790
A Japanese person?

468
00:51:15,130 --> 00:51:18,650
Hello. Yes.

469
00:51:32,800 --> 00:51:34,930
What does this mean?

470
00:51:34,930 --> 00:51:38,850
The ship arrived in Japan, but

471
00:51:38,850 --> 00:51:44,640
he said that the receiver of our container didn't show up.

472
00:51:44,640 --> 00:51:47,560
This... what is this supposed to mean?

473
00:51:47,560 --> 00:51:50,260
I'll contact the company in Japan and find out immediately.

474
00:51:50,260 --> 00:51:57,790
Hey, Gi Hoon. He said no such company exists.

475
00:51:57,790 --> 00:52:00,200
Pardon?

476
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:02,280
Honey, honey!!

477
00:52:04,580 --> 00:52:07,940
I'm okay... I'm okay.

478
00:52:07,940 --> 00:52:09,820
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

479
00:52:16,780 --> 00:52:21,490
It was a dummy company. All the documents were fake.

480
00:52:21,490 --> 00:52:26,470
Did you do this, Father? Was it you?

481
00:52:26,470 --> 00:52:28,570
It was Gi Jeong.

482
00:52:30,380 --> 00:52:32,160
Who?

483
00:52:32,160 --> 00:52:36,810
I just found it out now. It was Gi Jeong's doing.

484
00:52:59,610 --> 00:53:03,910
Hong Gi Hoon is on the line. Shall I put him through?

485
00:53:03,910 --> 00:53:07,510
- Put him through.
- I understand.

486
00:53:10,480 --> 00:53:12,920
It's me.

487
00:53:12,920 --> 00:53:15,680
Were you the one who did it?

488
00:53:15,680 --> 00:53:17,720
I don't know a bit of what you're saying,

489
00:53:17,720 --> 00:53:21,070
Did you want Dae Seong Cham Do Ga that much?

490
00:53:21,070 --> 00:53:24,870
Were you always this sneaky, Hyung Gi Jeong?

491
00:53:24,870 --> 00:53:30,330
I never imagined this from the eldest son of Hong Joo Ga Corporation.

492
00:53:30,330 --> 00:53:33,080
I didn't see you as someone who would take down someone's company

493
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:35,700
using an thug's underhanded trick like this.

494
00:53:35,700 --> 00:53:41,210
Was this really the action of Hong Gi Jeong, the eldest son of Hong Joo Ga corporation?

495
00:53:59,020 --> 00:54:02,930
Is this your family's doing?

496
00:54:08,070 --> 00:54:12,580
You've been in contact with your Hyung Gi Jeong?

497
00:54:13,530 --> 00:54:15,510
Ahjussi.

498
00:54:32,650 --> 00:54:36,140
Who's arguing to whom about being underhanded?

499
00:54:36,140 --> 00:54:39,050
I actually took a blow from you.

500
00:54:39,050 --> 00:54:43,530
I heard you used Father's money to buy that rice back. Congratulations.

501
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:48,300
For now, Dae Seong Cham Do Ga is going to be in yours and Father's hands.

502
00:54:48,300 --> 00:54:53,270
But don't let your guard down. I only did this as a test.

503
00:54:53,270 --> 00:54:57,690
If you take business so lightly, do you think you can last long?

504
00:55:11,330 --> 00:55:14,240
How could you...

505
00:55:14,240 --> 00:55:16,400
Ajusshi.

506
00:55:17,370 --> 00:55:22,860
How could you do this to me?

507
00:55:24,140 --> 00:55:26,100
Ajusshi.

508
00:56:47,920 --> 00:56:50,120
He passed away before you arrived.

509
00:56:50,120 --> 00:56:52,000
Be quiet.

510
00:56:52,920 --> 00:56:55,940
How dare you talk when you don't know anything?

511
00:56:58,440 --> 00:57:01,880
Honey. Joon Soo's dad...

512
00:57:01,880 --> 00:57:06,300
Honey.

513
00:57:50,250 --> 00:57:52,250
Dad...

514
00:57:58,810 --> 00:58:00,760
Mom.

515
00:58:03,720 --> 00:58:05,880
What happened to Dad?

516
00:58:08,360 --> 00:58:11,130
What happened to Dad?

517
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:19,190
Hyo Seon, wake your dad. Don't let him sleep.

518
00:58:37,470 --> 00:58:39,380
Dad.

519
00:58:45,210 --> 00:58:47,210
Dad.

520
00:58:50,450 --> 00:58:52,810
Hyo Seon is here.

521
00:59:10,080 --> 00:59:12,110
Dad.

522
00:59:18,870 --> 00:59:22,970
Where should I start first?

523
00:59:22,970 --> 00:59:28,790
No matter what, I want to do it all for you.

524
00:59:30,560 --> 00:59:33,570
You can rely on me.

525
00:59:33,610 --> 00:59:39,430
For the time being, I'll be the reason for you to stay here.

526
00:59:40,050 --> 00:59:46,030
I like him. So what? I like him. I like him because there's a lot I can take from him! Why?

527
00:59:46,030 --> 00:59:49,140
Don't abandon me.

528
00:59:49,140 --> 00:59:54,160
If you don't, I'll be grateful.

529
00:59:54,160 --> 00:59:59,210
Can you call me Dad just once?

530
01:00:01,690 --> 01:00:04,600
Dad, no!

531
01:00:04,600 --> 01:00:08,840
Dad! You can't! You can't. Dad.

532
01:00:12,400 --> 01:00:17,340
How can this happen?

533
01:00:17,340 --> 01:00:23,340
How can this happen?

534
01:00:26,960 --> 01:00:30,440
Stop it. Be quiet.

535
01:00:32,300 --> 01:00:34,820
Dad! Wake up!

536
01:00:34,820 --> 01:00:38,630
Be quiet, Hyo Seon. Stop it!

537
01:00:38,630 --> 01:00:40,430
Dad. Dad.

538
01:00:40,430 --> 01:00:44,140
What are you saying? Honey.

539
01:00:44,140 --> 01:00:50,380
- Dad, look at me.
- Get up right now, honey!

540
01:00:51,380 --> 01:00:54,190
Dad.

541
01:01:00,840 --> 01:01:04,900
I did this.

542
01:01:07,180 --> 01:01:13,550
I stole these two pretty girls' father away from them overnight.

543
01:01:15,250 --> 01:01:20,720
I swear...I didn't mean for this to happen.

544
01:02:01,470 --> 01:02:04,570
Can you call me Dad just once?

545
01:02:09,080 --> 01:02:12,470
You won't call me Dad?

546
01:02:16,800 --> 01:02:20,830
All right. I know you don't want to.

547
01:02:45,850 --> 01:02:48,640
- D...
- Dad!

548
01:02:48,660 --> 01:02:52,600
♫ It must be you ♫

549
01:02:52,600 --> 01:02:56,020
♫ I cannot be without you ♫

550
01:02:56,020 --> 01:03:02,920
♫ Like this for another day, month or year ♫

551
01:03:02,920 --> 01:03:06,580
♫ I don't mind even if I am hurt ♫

552
01:03:06,580 --> 01:03:10,580
♫ I don't mind even if my heart breaks ♫

553
01:03:10,580 --> 01:03:16,650
♫ because, yes, you are the only one I love ♫

554
01:03:16,700 --> 01:03:24,000
♫ My bruised heart is shouting so ♫

555
01:03:24,010 --> 01:03:29,190
♫ I can find you ♫

556
01:03:29,190 --> 01:03:32,840
♫ Wherever you are ♫

557
01:03:32,840 --> 01:03:36,660
♫ Can't you hear my voice? ♫
